From: hashtagbasit
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: bound the fence wait in msm_gem_vm_close()

An exiting gamescope on the AYN Thor got stuck in D state waiting on the
VM's last fence, became unkillable and blocked the next Game Mode start and
reboot. Wait at most 3 s, warn, and carry on with the teardown.

SteamOS-ARM-Port's 0009 (github.com/hashtagbasit/SteamOS-ARM-Port,
external-and-mods/kernel-sm8550/patches, added in 924a80f, by
hashtagbasit), not upstream, seen there on a Thor. vm->last_fence is the
last job of the VM's VM_BIND queue; when it never signals, the process
closing the device (the compositor, a game) is stuck unkillable here.
After 3 s the scheduler is stopped and torn down below with whatever
jobs it still holds, and the mappings are removed. Not yet tried on our
kernel.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_vma.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_vma.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_vma.c
index 2e16f3ebc..fdf1da145 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_vma.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem_vma.c
@@ -916,8 +916,16 @@ msm_gem_vm_close(struct drm_gpuvm *gpuvm)
 	if (vm->managed)
 		return;
 
-	if (vm->last_fence)
-		dma_fence_wait(vm->last_fence, false);
+	/*
+	 * Don't wait forever: on the AYN Thor an exiting gamescope sat here in
+	 * D state on a fence that never signalled, couldn't be killed, and
+	 * blocked the next Game Mode start and reboot. Give the GPU 3 s, then
+	 * tear down anyway (the scheduler is stopped right below).
+	 */
+	if (vm->last_fence &&
+	    dma_fence_wait_timeout(vm->last_fence, false, msecs_to_jiffies(3000)) <= 0)
+		pr_warn("msm: VM close: last fence %llu:%llu not signalled after 3 s\n",
+			vm->last_fence->context, vm->last_fence->seqno);
 
 	/* Kill the scheduler now, so we aren't racing with it for cleanup: */
 	drm_sched_stop(&vm->sched, NULL);
